{"created": "2026-10-17T17:44:20.489806+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-17T17:44:21.017669+00:00", "id": 23440119, "conceptrecid": "23440118", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23440119", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23440118", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23440119", "metadata": {"title": "A negative-curvature normal barrier on an algebraic cone that is not a hyperbolicity cone", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23440119", "publication_date": "2026-10-17", "description": "<p>An explicit affirmative answer to Tun\u00e7el's 2017 existential problem: the regular algebraic convex cone K={x,y,z\u22650:xy\u00b2\u2265z\u00b3} has the 100-normal barrier F=-25 log(z(xy\u00b2-z\u00b3)) with D\u00b3F(a)[h,u,u]\u22640 for every interior base point a, every cone direction h and every real direction u, but K is not the hyperbolicity cone of any homogeneous polynomial in the original three-dimensional space. The proof supplies exact polynomial and positive-semidefinite certificates for all directions, including degeneracies, and an arbitrary-degree boundary divisibility and nonreal-root obstruction.</p><p>Concise research note with TeX source, two independently authored standard-library exact verification programs, mathematical audits and a bounded primary-source priority audit. The underlying cone and known self-concordant power-cone barriers are credited to Hildebrand and Roy\u2013Xiao; the barrier parameter is deliberately nonoptimal. The broader every-regular-cone barrier question is outside the result. AI tools were used extensively in development, verification and writing. Unrefereed; no external human peer review or formal proof-assistant certification is claimed. The priority screen does not certify exhaustive literature coverage or first-ever priority.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kriebel, Alec", "affiliation": "Independent researcher", "orcid": "0009-0001-9320-500X"}], "keywords": ["convex optimization", "negative curvature", "self-concordant barriers", "normal barriers", "power cones", "hyperbolic polynomials", "Tun\u00e7el Open Problem 1"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.4171/owr/2017/14", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1412.1857", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.10263", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1305.4814", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://optimization-online.org/2018/01/6441/", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1108", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "1.0.0", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23440118"}}]}}, "title": "A negative-curvature normal barrier on an algebraic cone that is not a hyperbolicity cone", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23440119", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23440119", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23440119?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23440119", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23440119", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23440119", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23440119/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23440118", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23440118", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23440118", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23440118", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23440119/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23440119/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23440119/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records